---
import { skillFiles } from "../../../data/docs.ts";
import CopyButton from "../../ui/CopyButton.astro";

/**
 * AI skill. Describes skills/constitution/SKILL.md (front matter: name "constitution" plus the
 * trigger description) and its references/refusals.md. The files are served byte for byte from
 * web/public/skills/constitution/. Where your agent loads skills from is that agent's own setting, so
 * the page names no product or folder.
 */
const layout = skillFiles.map((file, index) => ({
  id: `docs-skill-path-${index}`,
  path: `constitution/${file.path}`,
}));
---

<div class="docs-prose">
  <p>
    A skill is a folder of instructions that a coding agent loads when a task matches it. This one is
    named <code>constitution</code>. It tells an agent how to write an upgrade for a
    CONSTITUTION-protected proxy, check it against R1 to R5, propose it to the demo gate, read the
    verdict or receipt, and explain a refusal such as R2/20, R1/10, R3/30 or R4/41. It covers the
    local checks, the honest VaultV2 and VaultV3 examples, demo submission and fail-closed recovery.
  </p>
  <p class="docs-note">
    <strong>It is a workflow, not a permission.</strong> The skill tells the agent to ask you for the
    applicable authorization before any write, to stay on testnet, never to read or print the contents
    of a key file and never to weaken a committed rule or a trusted reference to make a check pass.
  </p>

  <h3>Download</h3>
  <ul class="docs-downloads">
    {
      skillFiles.map((file) => (
        <li>
          <a class="docs-downloads__link" href={file.href} download>
            <span class="docs-downloads__name">{file.path}</span>
            <span class="docs-downloads__use">{file.purpose}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h3>Use it</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Download both files and keep them in one folder named <code>constitution</code>, with {" "}
      <code>refusals.md</code> inside a <code>references</code> folder beside {" "}
      <code>SKILL.md</code>, as in the layout below.
    </li>
    <li>
      Put that folder where your agent loads skills from. The location is your agent's own setting,
      so check its documentation.
    </li>
    <li>
      Open the agent in your checkout of the repository. The skill links to the committed rules, the
      deployment records and the guide by relative path, and it works best when they are there.
    </li>
    <li>
      Ask in plain words, for example: write an upgrade for the demo gate's vault, check this
      implementation against the five rules, or explain why a proposal was refused with R2/20.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="docs-paths">
    <p class="docs-label">Layout inside your agent's skills folder</p>
    <ul>
      {
        layout.map((entry) => (
          <li>
            <code id={entry.id}>{entry.path}</code>
            <CopyButton label="path" target={entry.id} />
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">
    The same two files are the repository's <code>skills/constitution/</code>. If your checkout has
    them, copy that folder instead of downloading.
  </p>
</div>
